{
  "summary": "The most likely cause of the WebUI going blank is the smartPollBoard() function (index.html:412-464) and smartPollFeatures() (client.html:529-612) — neither checks the HTTP response status before using the response body. If the server returns a non-200 response (500 error, timeout, empty body, or JSON error like {\"error\":\"...\"}), the code parses it as HTML, finds zero .stage-section elements, hits the branch `if (newSections.length !== curSections.length)`, and executes `container.innerHTML = html` — replacing the entire board with the error text or nothing. The fix is straightforward: add `if (!r.ok) return;` before processing the response text in both smartPollBoard and smartPollFeatures. Additionally, the htmx auto-refresh on the client cards div (hx-trigger='every 5s') has no error protection — htmx will swap in error responses by default, potentially blanking the clients grid too. A secondary concern is the service worker registration (sw.js) which could serve stale or cached error responses. The `.catch(function() {})` silent error swallowing is fine for network failures (it correctly does nothing), but the real gap is treating HTTP error responses as valid HTML content."
}
